Labels written for the single minimum-wage row (J.D. Mesnard). SCR1040 is a tipped-worker sub-minimum-wage (tip credit) constitutional amendment, which doesn't speak to the dimension the five served rungs order (indexing, legislative control, federalism, market-rate, or abolition of the general wage floor), so all three passages code `adjacent` and the row is `BLANK / no-evidence`.
